ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=housto
 nlinuxusergroup@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:houstonlinuxusergroup@gmail
 .com
CREATED:20260519T161550Z
DESCRIPTION:<span><p>Are you interested or already invested in the Linux Op
 erating System?<br>Join us at the Houston Linux User Group\, one of the old
 est user groups involved with the Linux Operating System. We discuss new tr
 ends in operating system usage\, software development\, and current technol
 ogical trends\, as well as provide one-on-one training or class-based instr
 uction. Learn about how to get more out of your computer or how to leverage
  any of the Linux-based computational platforms.<br>All are welcome to atte
 nd\, regardless of whether you’re a seasoned Linux professional intent on n
 etworking or a new Linux user struggling with installation or the command l
 ine.<br>This monthly meeting includes all of the standard Houston Linux Use
 r Group meeting activities\, which include meet-and-greet\, presentations o
 f personal projects\, multi-meeting classes\, as well as organizational and
  coordinating announcements.</p><p>Visit our website at: <a href="https://w
 ww.houstonlinux.org/" target="_blank">https://www.houstonlinux.org/</a><br>
 Visit our calendar at: <a href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/u/0/em
 bed?src=houstonlinuxusergroup@gmail.com" target="_blank">https://calendar.g
 oogle.com/calendar/u/0/embed?src=houstonlinuxusergroup@gmail.com</a></p><p>
 Join us on social media.<br>Discord: <a href="https://discord.gg/MPzYfeJz" 
 target="_blank">https://discord.gg/MPzYfeJz</a><br>Reddit: <a href="https:/
 /www.reddit.com/r/houstonlinuxusergroup/" target="_blank">https://www.reddi
 t.com/r/houstonlinuxusergroup/</a></p>Event link on Ion's website: <a href=
 "https://iondistrict.com/event/houston-linux-user-group-5/">https://iondist
 rict.com/event/houston-linux-user-group-5/</a><br> <br>Parking is free for 
 three hours\, we recommend that you not arrive too early or leave late.<br>
  <br>We encourage members to park at 4203 Fannin Street\, the "red" parking
  lot\, located across Fannin St. from the Ion. This lot is for guest and ev
 ent parking.  The smaller lot is intended for retail use.</span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260620T020907Z
LOCATION:The Ion\, Rooms 29 and 30\, 4201 Main St\, Houston\, TX 77002\, US
 A
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Houston Linux - Ion User Meeting
TRANSP:OPAQUE
