DESCRIPTION:<p>Edward Buck is going to present on Common Vulnerability Enum
 erations (CVE)</p><p>Ehsan Mohandesi is going to present the Persian Bingo 
 game he has created using GitHub Copilot. </p><p>Are you interested or alre
 ady invested in the Linux Operating System?<br>Join us at the Houston Linux
  User Group\, one of the oldest user groups involved with the Linux Operati
 ng System. We discuss new trends in operating system usage\, software devel
 opment\, and current technological trends\, as well as provide one-on-one t
 raining or class-based instruction. Learn about how to get more out of your
  computer or how to leverage any of the Linux-based computational platforms
 .<br>All are welcome to attend\, regardless of whether you’re a seasoned Li
 nux professional intent on networking or a new Linux user struggling with i
 nstallation or the command line.<br>This monthly meeting includes all of th
 e standard Houston Linux User Group meeting activities\, which include meet
 -and-greet\, presentations of personal projects\, multi-meeting classes\, a
 s well as organizational and coordinating announcements.</p><p>Visit our we
 bsite at: <a href="https://www.houstonlinux.org/" target="_blank">https://w
 ww.houstonlinux.org/</a><br>Visit our calendar at: <a href="https://calenda
 r.google.com/calendar/u/0/embed?src=houstonlinuxusergroup@gmail.com" target
 ="_blank">https://calendar.google.com/calendar/u/0/embed?src=houstonlinuxus
 ergroup@gmail.com</a></p><p>Join us on social media.<br>Discord: <a href="h
 ttps://discord.gg/MPzYfeJz" target="_blank">https://discord.gg/MPzYfeJz</a>
 <br>Reddit: <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/houstonlinuxusergroup/" targe
 t="_blank">https://www.reddit.com/r/houstonlinuxusergroup/</a></p>Event lin
 k on Ion's website: <a href="https://iondistrict.com/event/houston-linux-us
 er-group-4/" target="_blank">https://iondistrict.com/event/houston-linux-us
 er-group-4/</a><br> <br>Parking is free for three hours\, we recommend that
  you not arrive too early or leave late.<br> <br>We encourage members to pa
 rk at 4203 Fannin Street\, the "red" parking lot\, located across Fannin St
 . from the Ion. This lot is for guest and event parking.  The smaller lot i
 s intended for retail use.
